    <warningsAndCautions>
      <warning>
        <warningAndCautionPara>ISOLATE UNIT FROM ELECTRICAL POWER SUPPLY BEFORE ASSEMBLY. IF NOT INJURY CAN OCCUR.</warningAndCautionPara>
      </warning>
      <warning>
        <warningAndCautionPara>MAKE SURE THAT THE EQUIPMENT IS DE-ENERGIZED WHILE SERVICING. THIS WILL PREVENT INJURY TO PERSONNEL AND/OR DAMAGE TO THE COMPONENT.</warningAndCautionPara>
      </warning>
      <caution>
        <warningAndCautionPara>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS IN THE ASSEMBLY OF THE UNIT. WHEN YOU TORQUE THE BOLTS, SCREWS ETC., BE CAREFUL NOT TO CAUSE DAMAGE TO THE PANELS.</warningAndCautionPara>
      </caution>
      <caution>
        <warningAndCautionPara>DECORATIVE SURFACES MUST BE KEPT FREE OF DISCOLORATION, SCRATCHES, MARKS, AND DENTS.</warningAndCautionPara>
      </caution>
      <caution>
        <warningAndCautionPara>MOVE THE EQUIPMENT ASSEMBLIES BY SLIDING THEM ACROSS FLOOR SURFACES WILL DAMAGE THE TRACK ATTACHING FITTINGS OR MOUNTING SURFACES BY THE
ABRASIVE REMOVAL OF METAL FROM THESE CRITICAL AREAS. DAMAGE THE TRACK
ATTACHING FITTINGS OR MOUNTING SURFACES.</warningAndCautionPara>
